   "text": "The drawing is cholesterol (cholest-5-en-3\u03b2-ol). It has a four-ring steroid core, a C5=C6 double bond, a 3-OH, two angular methyl groups, and an 8-carbon branched side chain.\n\nI counted the atoms region by region:\n- **Ring A:** six-membered, with the OH on C3 and the double bond running from C5 to C6 in ring B.\n- **Rings B and C:** six-membered each, sharing the C8\u2013C9 and C13\u2013C14 fusions.\n- **Ring D:** five-membered, carrying the side chain at C17.\n- **Side chain:** C20 (with a methyl), then three more CH2 groups, then an isopropyl end (C25 with two methyls).\n- **Angular methyls:** one on C10 and one on C13.\n\nI checked the stereochemistry directly from the wedges and hashes at three centres:\n- **C3:** the wedged OH gives S.\n- **C10:** the wedged methyl gives R.\n- **C20:** the wedged methyl gives R.\n\nAll three match natural cholesterol. The hashed H atoms at C9 and C14 and the wedged H at C8 also fit the natural pattern, so I used the natural cholesterol stereo-SMILES.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H](CCCC(C)C)[C@H]1CC[C@@H]2[C@@]1(CC[C@H]3[C@H]2CC=C4[C@@]3(CC[C@@H](C4)O)C)C"
